KenshiLib_Examples_deps commit e75769b (pinned - see
third_party/KenshiLib_patches/README.md) defines `enum BuildingDesignation`
in BOTH kenshi/Building/Building.h and kenshi/Platoon.h (identical bodies -
a vendor copy-paste bug; Platoon.h even has a "// TODO move?" comment above
it). Any translation unit that includes both headers hits MSVC error C2011
'BuildingDesignation': 'enum' type redefinition. KenshiCoop's plugin does,
via EngineWorld.cpp and friends.

Fix: drop the duplicate from Platoon.h and #include Building.h there instead
(Building.h does not include Platoon.h, so no cycle).

Apply from the KenshiCoop repo root after fetching+pinning KenshiLib_deps
(see README.md in this folder for the fetch/checkout steps):

    git apply third_party/KenshiLib_patches/0001-fix-duplicate-buildingdesignation-enum.patch

--- a/third_party/KenshiLib_deps/KenshiLib/Include/kenshi/Platoon.h
+++ b/third_party/KenshiLib_deps/KenshiLib/Include/kenshi/Platoon.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <ogre/OgreMemoryAllocatorConfig.h>
 #include <ogre/OgreVector3.h>
 #include "Enums.h"
+#include "Building/Building.h"

 enum PlatoonCreationMessage
 {
@@ -27,22 +28,9 @@ class PatrolInfo;
 class AreaBiomeGroup;
 class AreaSector;

-// TODO move?
-enum BuildingDesignation
-{
-    BD_NONE,
-    BD_SHOP,
-    BD_BARRACKS,
-    BD_BAR,
-    BD_HOSPITAL,
-    BD_ARMOURY,
-    BD_TREASURE,
-    BD_PRISON,
-    BD_HQ,
-    BD_RESIDENTIAL,
-    BD_SLAVE_STORAGE,
-    BD_RESIDENTIAL_SMALL
-};
+// BuildingDesignation now comes from Building/Building.h (see #include above) -
+// this file used to redefine it here too, which is a C2011 duplicate-enum
+// error under a single-translation-unit build that includes both headers.

 enum BuildingFunction;

